Can confirm. It looks like the editors are sometimes getting more input events than they should, like they accumulate somewhere and suddenly one mouse left clicks sends up to 4 similar click events. For example, putting this code snipped in Polygon3DEditor::forward_3d_gui_input() shows input spam when adding points to CollisionPolygon3D. You can try editing, then removing all points and repeating and the input issue should soon become clear.

```
@@ -126,6 +126,11 @@ EditorPlugin::AfterGUIInput Polygon3DEditor::forward_3d_gui_input(Camera3D *p_ca
 	Ref<InputEventMouseButton> mb = p_event;
 
 	if (mb.is_valid()) {
+
+		if (mb->get_button_index() == MouseButton::LEFT) {
+			print_line("PRESS " + p_event->as_text() + " " + String::num_int64(mb->is_pressed()));
+		}
+
 		Vector2 gpoint = mb->get_position();
 		Vector3 ray_from = p_camera->project_ray_origin(gpoint);
 		Vector3 ray_dir = p_camera->project_ray_normal(gpoint);
```

